      "stem": "You are an F2 doctor on a respiratory ward. Mr Okafor, 46, was admitted yesterday evening with community-acquired pneumonia, and you clerked him. He has epilepsy, well controlled on levetiracetam twice daily.\n\nReviewing his drug chart on the morning ward round, you realise you did not prescribe his levetiracetam when you clerked him. He has missed last night's and this morning's doses. He has not had a seizure and is sitting up chatting to his wife. The nurse looking after him has not noticed the omission.",
