      "difficulty": "moderate",
      "stem": "You are an F2 doctor in a GP surgery. Mr Thompson, 79, has come for a review of his blood pressure medication. His daughter drove him to the appointment and has come into the room with him.\n\nEach time you ask Mr Thompson a question, his daughter answers for him. When you ask about side effects, she says, \"He gets muddled, it's easier if you just talk to me.\" There is no record of cognitive impairment in his notes. Mr Thompson looks at you, sighs, and says quietly that the new tablet makes him \"a bit dizzy when I get up in the morning\".",
