      "difficulty": "moderate",
      "stem": "You are an F2 doctor in general surgery. For the past three weeks, on the Tuesday day-case list, you have heard Mr Reid, a specialty doctor in your team, make sarcastic remarks to Ella, a newly qualified recovery nurse, about how \"slow\" she is. Today he did so in front of two patients who were waiting to go home.\n\nLater, you find Ella in the staff room. She looks upset. Mr Reid is generally well regarded and has been supportive of you during your placement.",
